WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.582
Manage tools as a small registry rather than handing every tool to the model.

00:00:06.582 --> 00:00:12.767
For each tool, store useful metadata: what kind of capability it provides, whether it is read-only,

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:17.378
a rough cost or latency class, and whether it requires approval.

00:00:18.061 --> 00:00:23.468
Consider three tools. Search knowledge is read-only and low risk.

00:00:23.468 --> 00:00:30.488
Get order is also read-only, but it accesses structured customer data and needs authorization.

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:38.523
Issue refund changes real-world state, so it should be treated very differently and probably require approval.

00:00:38.523 --> 00:00:45.046
A registry lets your controller filter which tools are even available for a particular task and user.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.262
Tool descriptions help the model choose.

00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:55.207
But permissions, approval, timeouts, and cost limits must be enforced outside the model.

00:00:55.207 --> 00:01:02.002
Also log tool name, validated arguments, duration, outcome, and error type.

00:01:02.002 --> 00:01:03.784
Do not log secrets.
